{"id":"neet-2026-q013","pn":13,"y":"NEET 2026 · 3 May","tp":"Wave Optics","st":"Intensity in Young's double slit","q":"In Young's double slit experiment, using monochromatic light of wavelength λ , the intensity of light at a point on the screen where the path difference is λ , is K units. The intensity of light at a point where the path difference is λ/3 will be","o":["(K)/(4)","K","(K)/(2)","2K"],"c":0,"s":"I = I₀cos²(Δφ/2), where I₀ is the maximum intensity.\nI = I₀cos²(KΔx/2), with wave number k = 2π/λ.\nFor path difference λ: K = I₀cos²((2π/λ) × (λ/2)) = I₀cos²π = I₀.\nFor path difference λ/3: K₁ = I₀cos²((2π/λ) × (λ/(3×2))) = I₀cos²(π/3).\nK₁ = I₀/4.\nSo K/K₁ = 4, which gives K₁ = K/4."},
{"id":"neet-2026-q034","pn":34,"y":"NEET 2026 · 3 May","tp":"Wave Optics","st":"Interference and diffraction","q":"In interference and diffraction, the light energy is redistributed. If it reduces in one region, producing a dark fringe, it increases in another region, producing a bright fringe.\nA. As there is no gain or loss of energy, these phenomena are consistent with the principle of conservation of energy.\nB. Diffraction and interference are characteristics exhibited only by light waves.\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:","o":["A is true, but B is false","A is true and B is also true","A is false, but B is true","Both A and B are false"],"c":0,"s":"In interference and diffraction there is no loss of energy; the energy only gets redistributed, so A is true.\nInterference and diffraction are shown by light waves as well as sound waves, so B is false."},
{"id":"neet-2025-q027","pn":27,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Wave Optics","st":"Polarisation, Brewster's law","q":"An unpolarized light beam travelling in air is incident on a medium of refractive index 1.73 at Brewster’s angle. Then","o":["Reflected light is completely polarized and the angle of reflection is close to 60°","Reflected light is partially polarized and the angle of reflection is close to 30°","Both reflected and transmitted light are perfectly polarized with angles of reflection and refraction close to 60° and 30°, respectively","Transmitted light is completely polarized with angle of refraction close to 30°"],"c":0,"s":"Use Brewster’s law: μ = tanθ_P.\n1.73 = tanθ_P.\n√3 = tanθ_P.\nθ_P = 60°.\nAt this polarising angle, the reflected light is perfectly polarized and the transmitted light is partially polarised.","sfig":{"w":330,"h":310,"alt":"Light incident on a medium of index 1.73 at 60 degrees; reflected ray completely polarised, 90 degrees between reflected and transmitted rays, transmitted ray at 30 degrees partially polarised","d":[["l",32,157,290,157],["l",136,15,136,285],["t",142,24,"N"],["l",65,48,136,157,"a"],["t",5,36,"Incident"],["t",14,52,"beam"],["l",136,157,230,82,"a"],["t",176,69,"(completely polarised)","s"],["t",176,56,"Reflected light","s"],["l",136,157,182,270,"a"],["t",105,108,"60°","s"],["t",146,108,"60°","s"],["t",176,187,"90°","s"],["t",184,167,"30°","s"],["t",242,203,"μ = 1.73"],["t",190,284,"Transmitted light","s"],["t",180,298,"(partially polarised)","s"],["p","M112 125 A 34 34 0 0 1 165 134"],["p","M170 154 A 34 34 0 0 1 150 188"],["l",34,172,288,172,"d"],["l",34,190,288,190,"d"],["l",34,208,288,208,"d"],["l",34,226,288,226,"d"],["l",34,244,288,244,"d"],["l",34,262,288,262,"d"]]}},
{"id":"neet-2025-q043","pn":43,"y":"NEET 2025","tp":"Wave Optics","st":"Polarisation, Malus law","q":"The intensity of transmitted light when a polaroid sheet, placed between two crossed polaroids at 22.5° from the polarization axis of one of the polaroids, is (I₀ is the intensity of polarised light after passing through the first polaroid):","o":["I₀/2","I₀/4","I₀/8","I₀/16"],"c":2,"s":"I₁ = I₀cos²(45/2).\nI₂ = I₁cos²(90 − 45/2).\nI₂ = I₀cos²(45/2) sin²(45/2).\nI₂ = (I₀/4)(4cos²(45/2) sin²(45/2)).\nI₂ = (I₀/4) sin²45° = I₀/8.","sfig":{"w":450,"h":190,"alt":"Light along a dotted axis through three polaroids: first axis vertical, second tilted 22.5 degrees from vertical, third at 90 minus 22.5 degrees; intensities I0, I1, I2","d":[["l",4,107,448,107,"d"],["l",45,36,45,180,"b"],["l",164,42,164,182,"d"],["l",130,175,201,36,"b"],["p","M164 63 A24 24 0 0 1 187 70"],["t",175,28,"22.5°"],["l",308,34,308,166,"d"],["l",279,166,323,74],["l",323,74,343,36,"d"],["l",256,82,386,140,"b"],["p","M323 76 A34 34 0 0 1 332 107"],["t",336,98,"90° − 22.5°"],["t",80,132,"I₀","s"],["t",226,132,"I₁","s"],["t",436,128,"I₂","s"]]}}
